    "name": "Blessed with Death",
    "steam_appid": 3210640,
    "required_age": 0,
    "is_free": true,
    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3210640/extras/4b0318899f8cf28ac0867b3d8b73d307.avif?t=1755544842\" data-has-big width=800 height=264 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3210640/extras/0f3634a5327e98fb14743460cf8eef72.poster.avif?t=1755544842\" width=780 height=438 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3210640/extras/0f3634a5327e98fb14743460cf8eef72.webm?t=1755544842\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3210640/extras/0f3634a5327e98fb14743460cf8eef72.mp4?t=1755544842\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >What sets the game apart from other FNAF-likes? </h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The Relics</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Every night you unlock new relics from which you always select one to help you get through the night. They grant effects such as resetting enemies and reviving you once upon death.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3210640/extras/49887033ad4279aa7e0f3bf37cff80f8.poster.avif?t=1755544842\" width=780 height=438 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3210640/extras/49887033ad4279aa7e0f3bf37cff80f8.webm?t=1755544842\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3210640/extras/49887033ad4279aa7e0f3bf37cff80f8.mp4?t=1755544842\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >No electricity</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There is no electricity in the game that you could use up, but that doesn't make it any easier because the door system has been adapted to this. Instead of simply using a switch to turn the light on and off as well as opening and closing the door, the player is required to hold it shut by themselves which forces them to stay at one place.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3210640/extras/46275b7a0f88232abfe4635686c6fa9d.poster.avif?t=1755544842\" width=780 height=438 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3210640/extras/46275b7a0f88232abfe4635686c6fa9d.webm?t=1755544842\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3210640/extras/46275b7a0f88232abfe4635686c6fa9d.mp4?t=1755544842\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Replay-ability</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >All enemies are randomly made more or less aggressive each time you start a night. So it's always a surprise who you have to pay special attention to. This means you have to adapt every night and quickly recognize the actual dangers.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3210640/extras/c1b79f0499aa00297eac75d9546399b2.avif?t=1755544842\" data-has-big width=800 height=264 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You desperately needed money, so you took the one job in the city that everyone avoided. Guarding an ancient house located deep in the forest. Where there is no road leading in or out.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >During the day, you don't have to be afraid. But at night, when the stars are favourable, they appear.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Now you fight for your survival on the edge of the world. Use magical objects that appear to be eons old and lock the doors. Every night, there are more and more of them.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >But you get to know them all better and learn about the past of this place. Search for clues and survive.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3210640/extras/fcfc805305e7c487dfca5531eb17de98.avif?t=1755544842\" data-has-big width=800 height=264 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Blessed with Death positions itself as a FNAF-Like, and we distance ourselves from the term FNAF-Fangame. The game has its own story, style and characters that are in no way connected to the FNAF world.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >We only based ourselves on the gameplay mechanics of the first FNAF games but changed them from the ground up.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Our game is of course oriented towards the existing community that is hungry for new secrets and gameplay mechanics.</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3210640/extras/4b0318899f8cf28ac0867b3d8b73d307.avif?t=1755544842\" data-has-big width=800 height=264 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3210640/extras/0f3634a5327e98fb14743460cf8eef72.poster.avif?t=1755544842\" width=780 height=438 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3210640/extras/0f3634a5327e98fb14743460cf8eef72.webm?t=1755544842\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3210640/extras/0f3634a5327e98fb14743460cf8eef72.mp4?t=1755544842\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >What sets the game apart from other FNAF-likes? </h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The Relics</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Every night you unlock new relics from which you always select one to help you get through the night. They grant effects such as resetting enemies and reviving you once upon death.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3210640/extras/49887033ad4279aa7e0f3bf37cff80f8.poster.avif?t=1755544842\" width=780 height=438 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3210640/extras/49887033ad4279aa7e0f3bf37cff80f8.webm?t=1755544842\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3210640/extras/49887033ad4279aa7e0f3bf37cff80f8.mp4?t=1755544842\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >No electricity</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There is no electricity in the game that you could use up, but that doesn't make it any easier because the door system has been adapted to this. Instead of simply using a switch to turn the light on and off as well as opening and closing the door, the player is required to hold it shut by themselves which forces them to stay at one place.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3210640/extras/46275b7a0f88232abfe4635686c6fa9d.poster.avif?t=1755544842\" width=780 height=438 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3210640/extras/46275b7a0f88232abfe4635686c6fa9d.webm?t=1755544842\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3210640/extras/46275b7a0f88232abfe4635686c6fa9d.mp4?t=1755544842\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Replay-ability</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >All enemies are randomly made more or less aggressive each time you start a night. So it's always a surprise who you have to pay special attention to. This means you have to adapt every night and quickly recognize the actual dangers.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3210640/extras/c1b79f0499aa00297eac75d9546399b2.avif?t=1755544842\" data-has-big width=800 height=264 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You desperately needed money, so you took the one job in the city that everyone avoided. Guarding an ancient house located deep in the forest. Where there is no road leading in or out.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >During the day, you don't have to be afraid. But at night, when the stars are favourable, they appear.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Now you fight for your survival on the edge of the world. Use magical objects that appear to be eons old and lock the doors. Every night, there are more and more of them.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >But you get to know them all better and learn about the past of this place. Search for clues and survive.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3210640/extras/fcfc805305e7c487dfca5531eb17de98.avif?t=1755544842\" data-has-big width=800 height=264 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Blessed with Death positions itself as a FNAF-Like, and we distance ourselves from the term FNAF-Fangame. The game has its own story, style and characters that are in no way connected to the FNAF world.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >We only based ourselves on the gameplay mechanics of the first FNAF games but changed them from the ground up.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Our game is of course oriented towards the existing community that is hungry for new secrets and gameplay mechanics.</p>",
    "short_description": "Guard a haunted house at night, protect yourself from intruders using magical relics and try to survive the nights in this unique FNAF-Like without electricity.",
